From: fxtec-pro1x-guix
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: repeated handover at debug level

On the Pro1x (SM6115) the ADSP raises its SMP2P ready and handover bits
again with every batch of an SSC sensor stream: 4.4 a second while
iio-sensor-proxy streams the accelerometer (smp2p-adsp interrupts 43 per
10 s with the stream, 0 without; wdog and fatal interrupts 0, the ADSP
stays up).  Each repeat logged "Handover signaled, but it already
happened" as an error, about 390000 lines a day.  Log it at debug level;
the first handover is handled as before.

Tested: interrupt counts on the phone (kernel 7.1.0, 8cd9520d); the patch
itself was not built locally (CI builds the kernel).
---
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -165,7 +165,12 @@
 	struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5 = data;
 
 	if (q6v5->handover_issued) {
-		dev_err(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
+		/*
+		 * The SM6115 ADSP raises its ready and handover bits again with
+		 * every batch of a sensor stream (several a second), so this is
+		 * not an error there.
+		 */
+		dev_dbg(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
